      "id": 116,
      "title": "APM status",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 71,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "End-to-end APM is partly wired, but current live Cloud Trace/APM proof must come from the post-deploy Grafana smoke. Expected server-side signals are API Cloud Run request spans, `otelpgx` DB spans, Cloud SQL infrastructure metrics, and pgx pool/query metrics; local guards only verify dashboard and smoke wiring. Pending Faro/RUM: the deployed admin-web revision must set `NEXT_PUBLIC_FARO_COLLECTOR_URL` before browser traces enter Alloy. Pending Cloud Trace dashboarding: the Cloud Trace datasource exists, but browser-to-API panels still need live Faro spans before they can prove a joined trace. Pending `traceparent` continuity: only selected admin-web proxy paths forward `traceparent`, and outbox producers still do not persist W3C `traceparent` into outbox headers, so producer write -> relay -> consumer is not one continuous trace yet."
      }
